# Agent-session roster — copy to .claude/agent-sessions.roster and edit.
# Read by the agent-sessions skill's launch-agent-sessions.sh. It can live in
# the target repo, or in a separate fleet repo that drives one or more target
# repos (then give every session an absolute <workdir>).
#
# Header (KEY=VALUE):
NAMESPACE=acme
# TMUX_SESSION=acme                      # default: NAMESPACE
# ENV_FILE=~/.config/acme/agents.env     # optional; sourced into every session
# MODEL=--model <model-id>               # optional; appended to every session
# PREFLIGHT=bash ~/bin/cloud-login.sh ~/.config/acme/agents.env   # optional,
# PREFLIGHT=gh auth status               # repeatable; fail-open identity checks
#
# Sessions: <name>|<workdir>|<initial prompt>|<extra flags>
#   name MUST start with "NAMESPACE-" — the messaging trust fence.
#   workdir empty → the directory the launcher runs from; ~ is expanded.
#   A fleet that keeps monster configs outside the repo passes the directory
#   in the initial prompt: /merge-monster fleet config dir: /abs/path
#
# Permission-mode guidance (full rationale: SKILL.md § Permission modes):
#   monsters (unattended)      → --dangerously-skip-permissions
#   edit-heavy interactive     → --permission-mode acceptEdits
#   read-heavy interactive     → (default gating)
acme-mm||/merge-monster|--remote-control --dangerously-skip-permissions
acme-maintain||/maintenance-monster|--remote-control --dangerously-skip-permissions
# Any further ledger-bearing role (its own skill + baton) is just another line;
# register it in fleet-supervisor.conf too so it is auto-relaunched:
# acme-<role>||/<role-skill>|--remote-control --dangerously-skip-permissions
acme-build|||--remote-control --permission-mode acceptEdits
acme-investigate|||--remote-control
acme-design|||--remote-control --permission-mode acceptEdits
